{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevRigidityMeromorphic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PeriodLatticeBasis","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_ratio_entire","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_ratio_entire","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly.lean#L44-L75","doc":"**Route-B assembly (concrete `Φ_b`).** For two `FaddeevPhi` solutions at `b`\nwith nondegenerate period lattice (`(b²).im ≠ 0`): if the ratio `r` is entire\n(`hr_entire`, the open bricks-b/c input) and equals `Φ₁/Φ₂` off `Φ₂`'s zeros\n(`hr_ratio`), and the loci `S₀, S₁` — where the respective prefactor is nonzero\n**and** `Φ₂` is nonzero at `z` and at its shift — are dense, then the two\nsolutions are proportional on `Φ₂`'s nonvanishing locus. The double periodicity\nof `r` is *derived* from `ratio_ib_periodic` / `ratio_ibinv_periodic`; only\n`hr_entire` and the locus density remain inputs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}